{"full":"hf:ra-led/depth-pro-normalized","spaceId":"ra-led/depth-pro-normalized","name":"depth-pro-normalized","source":"huggingface","description":"An interactive AI application on Hugging Face Spaces.","category":"AI & machine learning","language":"Python","topics":["gradio","region:us"],"technologies":["Python"],"likes":6,"created":"2024-10-28T09:02:05.000Z","updated":"2024-10-28T09:08:13.000Z","license":null,"runtime":"RUNNING","appUrl":"https://ra-led-depth-pro-normalized.hf.space/","demo":"https://huggingface.co/spaces/ra-led/depth-pro-normalized","availability":"available","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T11:06:18.175Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-08T11:06:18.175Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-08T11:06:18.175Z","color":"#3c3250","ink":"#e4d4ff","symbol":"🚀","overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["This software project accompanies the research paper: Depth Pro: Sharp Monocular Metric Depth in Less Than a Second, Aleksei Bochkovskii, Amaël Delaunoy, Hugo Germain, Marcel Santos, Yichao Zhou, Stephan R. Richter, and Vladlen Koltun.","We present a foundation model for zero-shot metric monocular depth estimation. Our model, Depth Pro, synthesizes high-resolution depth maps with unparalleled sharpness and high-frequency details. The predictions are metric, with absolute scale, without relying on the availability of metadata such as camera intrinsics. And the model is fast, producing a 2.25-megapixel depth map in 0.3 seconds on a standard GPU. These characteristics are enabled by a number of technical contributions, including an efficient multi-scale vision transformer for dense prediction, a training protocol that combines…","The model in this repository is a reference implementation, which has been re-trained. Its performance is close to the model reported in the paper but does not match it exactly."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://huggingface.co/spaces/ra-led/depth-pro-normalized/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"d2f7db60d7ebd09a7a499378b6d792afafad13a0